Hi Shadrielle,

The TitanCNA R package can handle both NCBI (1, 2, 3, ..., X, Y) and UCSC (chr1, chr2, chr3, ..., chrX, chrY) naming conventions.  You will need to modify the 2 specific lines in titan.R.  Please refer to Steps #6 and #7 in the instructions here: http://compbio.bccrc.ca/software/titan/titan-running-titancna/

In particular, you will want to use the argument
 genomeStyle = "UCSC"

Hope this helps.

Best,
Gavin

